# Power Query (M) Code — Revenue Analysis Model

**Companion file to `Revenue_BD5_Shell.xlsx`**

This file contains every Power Query you need to paste into the workbook's Power Query Editor. Queries are listed in the order they should be created. Each query loads to the Data Model only (right-click query → **Load To → Only Create Connection + Add to Data Model**).

---

## How to use this file

1. Open the workbook → **Data → Get Data → Launch Power Query Editor**
2. For each query below: **Home → New Source → Blank Query**, then **View → Advanced Editor**, paste the M code, click **Done**, name the query exactly as shown
3. After all queries are created: **Home → Close & Load To → Only Create Connection → Add this data to the Data Model**
4. Open Power Pivot (**Data → Manage Data Model**), create the relationships listed at the bottom of this file
5. Add the DAX measures (see workbook's "DAX Measures" tab)

---

## Setup — Parameters

Before pasting the queries, create a parameter for the source folder so the path lives in one place. **Home → Manage Parameters → New Parameter**:

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Name | `PMS_Source_Folder` |
| Type | Text |
| Suggested Values | Any value |
| Current Value | `https://yourtenant.sharepoint.com/sites/yoursite/Shared Documents/PMS_Exports/` |

Replace the URL with your actual SharePoint folder. If you're using a local file path, use the format `C:\Users\YourName\Folder\`.

