## Query 1: PMS_Raw

Loads every PMS export file in the source folder, combines them, and applies first-pass cleaning. Designed for a folder of monthly CSVs (one file per refresh).

```m
let
    // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    // Source: SharePoint folder containing PMS exports
    // (Swap SharePoint.Files for Folder.Files if loading from local drive)
    // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    Source = SharePoint.Files(PMS_Source_Folder, [ApiVersion = 15]),

    // Filter to CSV exports only (adjust extension to .xlsx if needed)
    FilterCSV = Table.SelectRows(Source, each Text.EndsWith([Name], ".csv")),

    // Combine all files in the folder into one table
    Combined = Table.Combine(
        List.Transform(
            FilterCSV[Content],
            each Csv.Document(_, [Delimiter = ",", Encoding = 65001, QuoteStyle = QuoteStyle.Csv])
        )
    ),

    // Promote headers
    Promoted = Table.PromoteHeaders(Combined, [PromoteAllScalars = true]),

    // Filter out any repeated header rows that appear after the first file
    NoRepeatedHeaders = Table.SelectRows(Promoted, each [Project_ID] <> "Project_ID"),

    // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    // Type the columns. Adjust the column names below to match
    // your actual PMS export column names exactly.
    // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    Typed = Table.TransformColumnTypes(NoRepeatedHeaders, {
        {"Date",            type date},
        {"Project_ID",      type text},
        {"Task",            type text},
        {"Consultant",      type text},
        {"Hours",           type number},
        {"Billable",        type text},
        {"Rate",            type number},
        {"Currency",        type text},
        {"Estimated_Total", type number}
    }),

    // Drop blank rows (no Project_ID or zero hours)
    NoBlanks = Table.SelectRows(Typed, each [Project_ID] <> null and [Hours] <> null and [Hours] <> 0),

    // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    // Derived columns used for joins and reporting
    // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    AddPeriod = Table.AddColumn(NoBlanks, "Period",
        each Date.ToText([Date], "yyyy-MM"), type text),

    AddYear = Table.AddColumn(AddPeriod, "Year",
        each Date.Year([Date]), Int64.Type),

    AddQuarter = Table.AddColumn(AddYear, "Quarter",
        each "Q" & Text.From(Date.QuarterOfYear([Date])), type text),

    // Join keys (text concatenations — match the bridge tables)
    AddCcyPeriod = Table.AddColumn(AddQuarter, "Currency_Period",
        each [Currency] & "|" & [Period], type text),

    // Normalize Billable flag — handles "Yes/No", "Y/N", "TRUE/FALSE", 1/0
    NormalizeBillable = Table.AddColumn(AddCcyPeriod, "Billable_Flag",
        each if [Billable] = null then "N"
             else if Text.Upper(Text.Start(Text.From([Billable]), 1)) = "Y" then "Y"
             else if Text.Upper(Text.Start(Text.From([Billable]), 1)) = "T" then "Y"
             else if [Billable] = "1" then "Y"
             else "N",
        type text),

    // Drop the original (string) Billable column to avoid confusion
    RemoveOriginal = Table.RemoveColumns(NormalizeBillable, {"Billable"}),
    RenameFlag = Table.RenameColumns(RemoveOriginal, {{"Billable_Flag", "Billable"}})

in
    RenameFlag
```

**Edit the column names** in the `Typed` step to match your PMS exactly. Common variations: `Hours_Logged`, `Bill_Rate`, `Project Code`, `Task Name`. Power Query is case-sensitive on column names.

