## Query 2: Project_Master

Loads the Project Master bridge table from the workbook.

```m
let
    Source = Excel.CurrentWorkbook(){[Name = "ProjectMaster"]}[Content],

    Typed = Table.TransformColumnTypes(Source, {
        {"Project ID",         type text},
        {"Client",             type text},
        {"Region",             type text},
        {"Product",            type text},
        {"Project Type",       type text},
        {"Internal/3rd Party", type text},
        {"Region_Product",     type text}
    }),

    Renamed = Table.RenameColumns(Typed, {
        {"Project ID",         "Project_ID"},
        {"Project Type",       "Project_Type"},
        {"Internal/3rd Party", "Internal_3rd_Party"}
    })
in
    Renamed
```

**Before loading:** In the workbook, select the data range on the **Project Master** tab (rows 5 onward, columns B–H), then **Formulas → Define Name → ProjectMaster** (or convert to an Excel Table named `ProjectMaster`). The query above looks for that named range / Table.

