## Query 5: Budget

Budget arrives wide (Region/Product as rows, months as columns) and needs to be unpivoted to long for the data model.

```m
let
    Source = Excel.CurrentWorkbook(){[Name = "BudgetTable"]}[Content],

    Typed = Table.TransformColumnTypes(Source, {
        {"Region",         type text},
        {"Product",        type text},
        {"Region_Product", type text}
    }),

    // Unpivot every month column. The "unpivotOther" approach catches all
    // remaining columns regardless of how many months are in the table.
    Unpivoted = Table.UnpivotOtherColumns(
        Typed,
        {"Region", "Product", "Region_Product"},
        "Period",
        "Budget_USD"
    ),

    BudgetTyped = Table.TransformColumnTypes(Unpivoted, {
        {"Period",     type text},
        {"Budget_USD", type number}
    }),

    AddKey = Table.AddColumn(BudgetTyped, "Region_Product_Period",
        each [Region_Product] & "|" & [Period], type text)
in
    AddKey
```

Define name `BudgetTable` on the Budget tab.

