## Data Model Relationships

Open Power Pivot (**Data → Manage Data Model**), switch to **Diagram View**, drag-and-drop to create:

| From | To | Cardinality |
|---|---|---|
| `Fact_Table[Project_ID]` | `Project_Master[Project_ID]` | Many → One |
| `Fact_Table[Currency_Period]` | `FX_Rates[Currency_Period]` | Many → One |
| `Fact_Table[Region_Product_Period]` | `Budget[Region_Product_Period]` | Many → One |
| `Project_Master[Region_Product]` | `Region_Product_Map[Region_Product]` | Many → One |

If you also have a Date dimension table (recommended for time intelligence), create:
| `Fact_Table[Date]` | `Date[Date]` | Many → One |

