## Performance notes for ~700MB data volume

- **Disable auto-detection of relationships and types** in Power Query options to speed loads
- **Set `Table.Buffer` on bridge tables only** if joins are slow — don't buffer Fact_Table
- **Don't load Fact_Table to a worksheet** under any circumstance. Worksheets cap at ~1M rows and would balloon the file
- **Use the `xlsb` format for the final workbook** if file size becomes an issue — same data model, much smaller footprint
- **Refresh order**: Bridge tables first (FX, Project Master, Region Map, Budget), then PMS_Raw, then Fact_Table. Power Query usually handles this automatically via dependency graph
- **For incremental refresh**: if Pro/Premium dataset, configure incremental refresh to only re-pull recent months rather than the full 2-year history every BD1

